irements">Requirements</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"#HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewithIGELOS12Devices-Fall=
backBehaviorwithRepositories">Fallback Behavior with Repositories</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"#HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewithIGELOS12Devices-Reco=
mmendedConfiguration-IntendedUseCase">Recommended Configuration - Intended =
Use Case</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"#HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewithIGELOS12Devices-HowI=
GELDiscoveryWorksb1e51364-5b6b-4d7d-8a32-a9f03691a506">How IGEL Discovery W=
orks</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"#HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewithIGELOS12Devices-Prox=
yConsiderations">Proxy Considerations</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"#HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewithIGELOS12Devices-Alte=
rnativeConfigurations">Alternative Configurations</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"#HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewithIGELOS12Devices-Furt=
herInformation">Further Information</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
<h2 local-id=3D"7adca356065a" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-LimitationsandKnownIssues">Limitations and Known Issues</h2=
>
<h3 local-id=3D"d08adb7dc055" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-CommunityApplicationsNotSupportedYet">Community Application=
s Not Supported Yet</h3>
<p local-id=3D"6fb255958747">Currently, community applications are not supp=
orted by Distributed Peer Update. Including a community application in an u=
pdate can break the entire update process. Fixes are planned to be added wi=
th a future IGEL OS 12 release.</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-not=
e">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-warning confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"7d358b3a3d34">Do not use Distributed Peer Update for updates=
 that include community applications until fixes are available.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"b59db917fc3b" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-HTTPSNotSupportedYet">HTTPS Not Supported Yet</h3>
<p local-id=3D"2604dacaf22f">Currently, the communication for the Distribut=
ed Peer Update is done through HTTP by default. HTTPS support is planned to=
 be added with a future IGEL OS 12 release.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"6c894385a6e4" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-Components">Components</h2>
<p local-id=3D"4df609a98c06">Peer-to-peer distribution relies on two compon=
ents that run on IGEL OS devices:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"67b4a98c-5dfc-441c-b7c3-b20b74a354d9">
<li local-id=3D"01f20e00-b524-403b-98e0-4f4a36365ff4">
<p local-id=3D"595afff69e52">IGEL Discovery</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0472a0e3-437e-4c3f-8036-fe4ad2bb7092">
<p local-id=3D"d88fb7d9fdfe">Distributed Peer Update Server (=E2=80=9CBuddy=
=E2=80=9D)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"62c09102e20e">Together, these components allow peer-to-peer =
distribution of applications and updates within the same subnet.</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1015" data-layout=3D"align-start" data-local-id=
=3D"013ec078-e277-4d81-a6fe-d0b009562cf6" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 207.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 302.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 303.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 202.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"73daabab-5f10-4a83-8c37-901b917116a7">
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"8085f92a-f513-402d-9=
a96-1b27aea0d306" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"233638803581"><strong>Component</strong></p></th>
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"a16ac233-b8d7-4246-a=
20c-82bdf865afce" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"cc39267d4b40"><strong>Description</strong></p></th>
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"8b23b1e5-070f-4154-b=
01a-4e962a9689b1" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"dad1da905241"><strong>Network Traffic Types</strong></p></th=
>
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"6e9b1112-092b-48e3-a=
35a-1601c226f37d" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"4db6de9f038e"><strong>Configuration</strong></p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"efe4a05b-0521-4a64-9cbd-b8bd2a5dc41e">
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"0748b06f-59b2-49bd-b=
298-52efd5092687" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"b573395add60"><strong>IGEL Discovery</strong></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"8d16c43d-d0be-4b02-a=
7a6-0605abca6b07" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"0db0afaea91a">Zero-configuration peer discovery service that=
 automatically discovers peers that already have applications available. It=
 also decides if a device that should download from a repository if no peer=
 has the application.</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"b286d2ce-6569-413c-9=
f38-b5a6cb06f522" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"1ce931ec3656">IGEL Discovery works only within the same broa=
dcast domain. The Discovery uses:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"273adcba-e714-437e-99e8-08dc7f7660df">
<li local-id=3D"458592c1-4e4a-4133-b5af-b6e26d53270b">
<p local-id=3D"240709e5d877">UDP broadcast requests within the local subnet=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"771dbcb9-9caf-4839-9780-9079cd6c0546">
<p local-id=3D"e72f51410c82">UDP unicast for responses between devices</p><=
/li>
</ul></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"ff410229-e24e-4229-8=
fb1-d26f10cdeec1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"519bf7646214"><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://kb.=
igel.com/en/igel-os-base-system/current/igel-discovery-service-configuratio=
n-in-igel-os" rel=3D"nofollow"><strong>System &gt; Update &gt; IGEL Discove=
ry</strong></a></p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"58271526-a2c9-4681-8120-f70995e2aab2">
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"b38961a5-4f31-4e28-a=
b82-b823596ed6b1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"caecee4e4a4c"><strong>Distributed Peer Update Server (=E2=80=
=9CBuddy=E2=80=9D)</strong></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"680800ab-a873-42ee-8=
a7a-a29fe9169c61" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"6b219d6a75b6">HTTP server running on the device that provide=
s applications and updates to other IGEL OS devices.</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"b8baae2f-e3f7-4a74-9=
13b-09cdf968c76a" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"8bb614091cc8">HTTP peer transfers</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"02a00873-944c-4b90-8=
9e0-2c0369e8884f" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"d9129cf5bbb1"><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://kb.=
igel.com/en/igel-os-base-system/current/distributed-peer-update-server-conf=
iguration-in-ig" rel=3D"nofollow"><strong>System &gt; Update &gt; Distribut=
ed Peer Update Server</strong></a></p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h2 local-id=3D"61171909bee5" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-Requirements">Requirements</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"a477becb1e48" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-IGELOSVersion">IGEL OS Version</h3>
<p local-id=3D"070622120b2e">IGEL OS 12 devices need to run IGEL OS Base Sy=
stem version 12.7.4 or higher.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"58848c093a09" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-PortRequirements">Port Requirements</h3>
<p local-id=3D"b0431fd9bb59">The IGEL Discovery service and the Distributed=
 Peer Update Server use separate ports, as described in the table below:</p=
>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"934" data-layout=3D"align-start" data-local-id=
=3D"bfdbde85-1878-4356-b7d4-b7594838afe8" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 307.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 135.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 186.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 301.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"62b4346a-4ee6-407f-8221-6ee5a1e94507">
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"e766730d-8168-4f32-a=
74d-cdb96f292287" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"568c90d5d099"><strong>Service</strong></p></th>
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"daf22c5c-f840-4ccf-a=
a6c-1e278b224e94" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"0524fa784644"><strong>Protocol</strong></p></th>
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"ad2b9c63-489e-40bb-b=
fcb-ec049b855ba7" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"3a970549278e"><strong>Default Port</strong></p></th>
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"8e5b8123-35ce-46bd-8=
a1b-99b0c28f3f30" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"e48ad88e0b6f"><strong>Configuration</strong></p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"ed9c9108-0225-48e4-b331-80509c2eb976">
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"4c2bf261-b900-4272-9=
d67-20c67f6933bb" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"623ceca559e8"><strong>IGEL Discovery</strong></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"add305e7-4699-49e1-b=
4f0-0ae6b0df8f84" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"f6f357b0bdaf">UDP</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"cbc6a61d-6b29-4bd4-a=
73a-223cb785a979" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"85b9291d8366"><code>22336</code></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"029e539c-0ee6-4f8b-a=
1ab-f3f8d7b476c3" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"0dc5e5728a77"><strong>System &gt; Update &gt; IGEL Discovery=
 &gt; Port</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"f59bbca7-8a9a-4ee3-b378-044ef24b2bdf">
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"1825baae-906b-4278-a=
f84-2beb01e09fb4" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"6a54961bba1c"><strong>Distributed Peer Update Server</strong=
></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"d09e7beb-e0a9-448f-a=
b65-abd571663273" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"27c5b101cf37">HTTP</p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"d0402662-4f83-44ee-8=
2e1-b9ac42b8887c" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"e9ba097a65fc"><code>22335</code></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"7a76bbb8-aaa9-4921-9=
003-1684b4df7ecc" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"bff15f179b5f"><strong>System &gt; Update &gt; Distributed Pe=
er Update Server &gt; Port of the distributed peer update server</strong></=
p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"172111e86060">When configuring the ports, consider the follo=
wing:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"3a832776-0054-461f-840d-8fcf579c519f">
<li local-id=3D"6b8c7616-24bb-4861-b625-9991af3fc499">
<p local-id=3D"a36fe0036305">The Distributed Peer Update Server and the IGE=
L Discovery service must run on different ports.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b9b2d950-b5b6-49de-9ee8-0a21d25b7da9">
<p local-id=3D"9b5975de01cc">The same Discovery port must be configured on =
all devices that should discover each other.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5e71f7e8-e31e-44db-b361-43c012ca85e6">
<p local-id=3D"ec646dfcf8de">The same Distributed Peer Update Server port m=
ust be configured on all devices that should act as peers for each other.</=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"28272c8c-8914-4bc1-8353-ec1f52966a16">
<p local-id=3D"42b146f369ee">The configured ports must be open and allowed =
by any host firewall on the endpoint and by any network firewalls between d=
evices.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"3856fde2ecf4" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-NetworkRequirements">Network Requirements</h3>
<p local-id=3D"0f9ee8fcd2e7">Some network configurations may prevent discov=
ery from working correctly. In these environments, devices may not be able =
to discover peers automatically.</p>
<p local-id=3D"838c0a479df1">For example:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"971ab438-6079-470a-adae-98602685fe0c">
<li local-id=3D"b1561a68-10ba-4ced-a389-38161abe29ff">
<p local-id=3D"3698a8edcdc8">Wi-Fi networks with client isolation</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9464507d-28f6-4c3e-adaa-aa845955da2d">
<p local-id=3D"acfa027a51f8">Networks that block broadcast traffic</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"9b96cf2b815b" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-FallbackBehaviorwithRepositories">Fallback Behavior with Re=
positories</h2>
<p local-id=3D"75744d184964">Peer-to-peer distribution relies on IGEL Disco=
very to locate a device that already has the requested application. If no d=
evice in the subnet can provide the application, Discovery elects one devic=
e to download the application from a configured repository. This device bec=
omes the fallback candidate. Once the application is downloaded and install=
ed, the device can serve it to other devices as the Distributed Peer Update=
 Server.</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"09cbb7709d34">No reboot is required for the Distributed Peer=
 Update Server to start distributing newly received applications. As soon a=
s an application is installed, it can be served to peers.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"dc8cc397581b">The fallback device downloads the application =
from the repository with the highest priority that contains the application=
. Supported repository types include:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"177f9190-751f-47a8-a4e3-d648f48037ce">
<li local-id=3D"996c704d-8c60-427e-9e3d-0220a07713af">
<p local-id=3D"206f5b8175f9">UMS App Proxy</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"637361bd-2849-4e65-b950-ea553089217f">
<p local-id=3D"b561d0c77213">WebDAV repositories</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"85727222-e411-4939-973d-f7718a3000f4">
<p local-id=3D"2f17960ea230">IGEL App Portal</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"82be25c2-81ef-4505-a11a-cddf717d9862">
<p local-id=3D"7c83748909f6">Other repositories configured under <a class=
=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://kb.igel.com/en/igel-os-base-system/curre=
nt/update-app-update-settings-in-igel-os-12" rel=3D"nofollow"><strong><u>Sy=
stem &gt; Update &gt; Repositories</u></strong></a></p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"6ce765b038aa" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-CanFallbackBeDisabled?">Can Fallback Be Disabled?</h3>
<p local-id=3D"536c86ae735c">There is no direct setting to disable the fall=
back, because at least one device (the first device of the subnet) must obt=
ain the application from a repository. However, repository usage is limited=
 to the first download within a subnet.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e08f84783b7c">Once a device has downloaded the application:<=
/p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"52fbc512-db62-4c20-9519-92e406d1f15e">
<li local-id=3D"8b9c8c10-b299-4d0b-82e9-79d775dfd4e2">
<p local-id=3D"959487e48a5c">The device can serve the app to other peers if=
 it is configured as Distributed Peer Update Server.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"88fd3988-4a89-4dec-8e97-70b276a27d1b">
<p local-id=3D"722f28e5f269">IGEL Discovery detects the available peer.</p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"45ade7b7-fbf8-4a14-9fbb-f512201bb508">
<p local-id=3D"5ce1e74d675d">Other devices download the application directl=
y from the peer instead of the repository.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"c831d947d26f" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-RecommendedConfiguration-IntendedUseCase">Recommended Confi=
guration - Intended Use Case</h2>
<p local-id=3D"ea7b7aa73495">The intended use case is to operate Distribute=
d Peer Update as a peer=E2=80=91to=E2=80=91peer network, where all devices =
both discover and serve updates.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b869f27cad2c">To do this, you can configure devices through =
profiles:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"edec5a7c-e5b8-4b3f-99ec-8a849625f8a5">
<li local-id=3D"557fd04c-4c2d-4721-a297-9f9d3934cc90">
<p local-id=3D"bcb637e5049b">Create a profile.<br></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0ef89d33-8a1c-4cc6-8975-1844f0f31ef3">
<p local-id=3D"0885a4f00e8f">In the profile configurator, configure IGEL Di=
scovery and Distributed Peer Update Server on all devices according to the =
table:</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"831" data-layout=3D"align-start" data-local-id=
=3D"9dd59aa3-af11-4331-9e85-499e2116d6cd" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 279.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 275.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 277.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"d67bc6d5-480d-47c6-b196-7f8939ab0845">
