<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"cd1976d5-0217-4fc1-8=
168-a831285fd8dc" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"440ddab215e8"><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://kb.=
igel.com/en/igel-os-base-system/current/distributed-peer-update-server-conf=
iguration-in-ig" rel=3D"nofollow"><strong>System &gt; Update &gt; Distribut=
ed Peer Update Server</strong></a></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"a280d24a-da94-4082-9=
c29-0ba68cececd1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"d6d49697bfaf"><strong>Port of the distributed peer update se=
rver</strong></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"23aa7629-1902-4630-9=
e62-d8894fcd4947" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"5810acb3cbd9">Same on all devices (default <strong>22335</st=
rong>)</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<ol start=3D"3" local-id=3D"e7f701de-a6d7-491c-a4a9-447c4b39d078">
<li local-id=3D"c1f3ca7f-88b9-44fb-b4d4-f9d335dfea10">
<p local-id=3D"40731446c7c5">Save and assign the profile to the devices.</p=
></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"42bcb9e054ad">With this configuration:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"3d69c34e-a08e-4936-94a9-9aefd1d982a6">
<li local-id=3D"0cfc579b-e108-48a6-897a-db65652f5d63">
<p local-id=3D"d4eb469105dd">You can assign applications to devices without=
 considering server roles.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3b2cb661-9af1-49b4-bfed-52d03d4075c4">
<p local-id=3D"81c12d6cc344">Discovery ensures that only one device at a ti=
me in a subnet uses the fallback to fetch the application from a repository=
.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"07560c7d-7dab-4012-8568-43e0f20c4426">
<p local-id=3D"1bb51afce063">Once a device that is configured as a Distribu=
ted Peer Update Server has the application, it becomes a peer server for ot=
her devices.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ae97f549-150c-42ec-b2f5-a3e94a7bf421">
<p local-id=3D"ab801abbcfa2">The distribution speed ramps up quickly due to=
 exponential growth:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"8c580fc8-0484-41c0-a58d-e825c705e287">
<li local-id=3D"babcb532-1384-446c-b4e5-f089477dfe8a">
<p local-id=3D"3ef06efa95d7">1 Distributed Peer Update Server with the appl=
ication =E2=86=92 1 device can download and become Peer Update Server</p></=
li>
<li local-id=3D"01f7be80-bc94-484f-b787-8266ae25d4c9">
<p local-id=3D"4fff0b8594a8">2 Distributed Peer Update Servers =E2=86=92 2 =
devices can download and become Peer Update Server</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a3d2e28b-c4f3-458b-bdb2-6f4eaa2940d3">
<p local-id=3D"4f2c6b4a4dfa">4 Distributed Peer Update Servers =E2=86=92 4 =
devices can download and become Peer Update Server</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ef504835-ef92-4fc6-b7b6-81d22fb44649">
<p local-id=3D"ce49114e9b32">8 Distributed Peer Update Servers =E2=80=A6 an=
d so on =E2=80=A6</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"fe2f9aac8a36" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-RolloutConsiderationsforLargeEnvironment">Rollout Considera=
tions for Large Environment</h3>
<p local-id=3D"f1f5fb26dfb1">In very large environments or networks with li=
mited bandwidth, application deployments can be performed in waves as a bes=
t practice.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e7150732d15e">Example rollout:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"41df5c0a-7ef1-4b58-bf9e-9761ae244290">
<li local-id=3D"14276be0-e17a-4023-a414-89a9caa060ae">
<p local-id=3D"4327493db48e">First wave: 100 devices</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e52632be-a6b6-4342-898e-fae2201e18bd">
<p local-id=3D"aceca6cfa321">Second wave: next 100 devices</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c31963a8-8b9d-4583-bce9-7771701a4f60">
<p local-id=3D"2fb8f1c3e815">Third wave: remaining devices</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"958c3ee06882">This prevents excessive simultaneous downloads=
 and reduces network congestion.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"0bea3419ce6d" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-HowIGELDiscoveryWorksb1e51364-5b6b-4d7d-8a32-a9f03691a506">=
How IGEL Discovery Works<span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"HowtoC=
onfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewithIGELOS12Devices-b1e51364-5b6b-4d7d-8a32-a9=
f03691a506"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"b1e51364-5b6b-4d7d=
-8a32-a9f03691a506"></span></span></h2>
<p local-id=3D"2e5443cd3321">Once IGEL Discovery and Distributed Peer Updat=
e are enabled, application distribution is automated.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"0535334073f0" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-DistributionProcess">Distribution Process</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"0c423fd8-877c-4072-ae32-326c4f357275">
<li local-id=3D"ca7f8cc8-81a0-4d52-bbff-6196c216b805">
<p local-id=3D"68adcbfe4284">A management system (for example UMS) assigns =
an application to a device.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a9fe493d-e0e1-44b1-b6b4-af2271003143">
<p local-id=3D"8ead4ceea934">The device=E2=80=99s update daemon checks whet=
her Discovery is enabled.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"611dbb53-5f8e-4fe7-bf9f-1900a5ff9a03">
<p local-id=3D"ec78d34279df">If Discovery is enabled, the update daemon ask=
s Discovery to find a peer with the requested application.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a41b18f5-8962-4630-b130-fa8fab1fe6da">
<p local-id=3D"52e10f2f8126">IGEL Discovery broadcasts a UDP request within=
 the subnet asking for the application.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0ae305c5-372e-41f5-9440-4061a91a0599">
<p local-id=3D"6a78c9738d0e">Devices respond depending on their state.</p><=
/li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"4ce0519e11ee" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-DiscoveryResponses">Discovery Responses</h3>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"align-start" data-local-id=
=3D"da42d98a-cf03-48c4-afc8-68f8c9157583" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 176.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 583.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"c31800c2-c9d2-4f9d-b2e0-5b66eca70ef7">
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"94f241a8-e8d3-45f8-8=
001-f474ffd607da" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"2f206b55b037">Response</p></th>
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"cee4c13a-be01-410a-a=
4e1-f48139636c85" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"2d24f39f028e">Meaning</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"60b176e7-1063-4d74-8260-f9ae79eec59c">
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"77b4b07f-0220-4358-9=
af5-075c56953d84" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"d5d481634d7a"><code>SERVER_READY</code> via UDP unicast</p><=
/td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"081289de-f932-4d17-8=
2d6-d01f05dc1a1b" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"90a504944302">A peer has the application and is ready to ser=
ve it</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"7fd84b0a-a0c7-4d05-8df0-5d7f8ce5558d">
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"ab25fae6-d81a-4cd0-8=
d1a-f70c971811e1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"2181aae004c2"><code>SERVER_BUSY</code> via UDP broadcast</p>=
</td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"f078cdc5-960d-4ba8-b=
1c7-32d5995f7dbd" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"4a0254e1c342">A peer has the application but is currently se=
rving another download</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"e59ce707-0c62-405f-bc1e-13fb644fe83c">
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"1e5c89a1-679e-40b9-9=
9f9-53eed4397f1d" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"e7ce958af2a9"><code>FALLBACK</code></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"0ddeece0-740c-4316-8=
a7a-35cf9f4224ef" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"78b09688f89a">No peer has the application; a device must dow=
nload from a repository</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-tip=
">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-approve confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"1588060d6366">To view IGEL Discovery responses, run:</p>
<p local-id=3D"27d77ad55463"><code>journalctl -u igel-discovery-daemon -f</=
code></p>
</div>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"3797d8ec152c" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-UpdateDaemonBehavior">Update Daemon Behavior</h3>
<p local-id=3D"77cda46ee5cf">The update daemon reacts to Discovery response=
s as follows.</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"align-start" data-local-id=
=3D"0c33317f-d909-42a1-8e1c-1394024abbe9" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 200.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 558.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"2707354a-9d6c-4f77-b0fc-958579761050">
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"cc3ca77e-286f-44e0-a=
26e-fa8f87374802" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"8031406effb8">Discovery Response</p></th>
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"bc8e6716-d735-4e6e-b=
528-e9aa28bae605" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"98dd2dc01a6b">Behavior of the Update Daemon</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"d153d519-1280-45dd-b206-9da9ebdc46c2">
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"e8299779-29f1-451a-a=
4b7-3670f6723f3e" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"d7fa098a5c61"><code>SERVER_READY</code></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"1f5b4322-276a-4eca-a=
e12-9e7d3b0d886e" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"3c138513537c">Downloads the application from the peer=E2=80=
=99s Distributed Peer Update Server over HTTP.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"3dceef4a-ba5f-4935-92c7-9a7237dcae5a">
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"2da1d249-c4e1-4f7d-9=
29d-cf3fe69d7694" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"51d95595803a"><code>SERVER_BUSY</code></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"bfa987ae-90f1-4442-8=
e9d-effc65546753" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"a63d9edcdc38">The update daemon waits and retries in an infi=
nite loop, with a wait time (for example 100 seconds) between search rounds=
.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"e9b0a7ce-d8c6-4d5f-941a-fe606bf76007">
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"ef32cf7a-aa27-4969-b=
ae2-4332db8f2915" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"763b3935e13d"><code>FALLBACK</code></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"6d8413a2-3d41-4ab7-8=
a7a-ae5b3fb04c38" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"721aea71e522">The device elected as fallback downloads the a=
pplication from the repository (UMS app proxy, WebDAV, IGEL App Portal, and=
 so on). Once downloaded and installed, this device can serve the applicati=
on to others via its Distributed Peer Update Server.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"3cd0d43209b0" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-UpdateProgressIndicatorBehavior">Update Progress Indicator =
Behavior</h3>
<p local-id=3D"690406f58ab4">During peer discovery and fallback selection, =
the update progress indicator may temporarily remain at <strong>0%</strong>=
.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2972805da15e">This can occur while:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"7f48d272-77ed-4ca7-8f01-b072192e10ea">
<li local-id=3D"31090ffd-f53a-4be9-b25a-77dc9116cd19">
<p local-id=3D"ea1d932c6790">Discovery searches for a peer server</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2f7d6b76-df29-4332-bed4-546ef1de9668">
<p local-id=3D"cfccb20e787c">A fallback device downloads the application</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"d9c08311-f17c-426f-9b61-f7af3088fbd0">
<p local-id=3D"64f2ac7eef8f">A peer disappears (for example powered off, ne=
twork loss) and the update daemon has to request another server.</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"3e9d640f31b8">Once a peer becomes available, the download pr=
oceeds normally.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"18c859b34784" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-ProxyConsiderations">Proxy Considerations</h2>
<p local-id=3D"aebaaf47fe10">IGEL Discovery and the update daemon behave di=
fferently when a proxy is configured.</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"align-start" data-local-id=
=3D"a80c8bf4-6121-40bb-be7f-30a8c05e7729" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"63125512-af09-421f-bce7-3095150e8821">
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"fbf77f26-a3f9-41fd-9=
bb7-ede7f3dbabdd" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"f0cc9d5191f6">Component</p></th>
<th data-highlight-colour=3D"#f0f1f2" data-local-id=3D"2cab4d36-65a7-4a3d-9=
efe-18e69245d446" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"b6472846f6a7">Proxy Behavior</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"ac4d71e4-3665-44c2-828b-8dcf9bd15020">
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"deca3dc2-fff4-4276-8=
029-5c1df4611810" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"169a6798adf3"><strong>IGEL Discovery</strong></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"dd1b0b2d-6cb6-46d1-a=
e41-aeb3753c0f80" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"da5288083589">Bypasses HTTP proxy configuration because it u=
ses UDP broadcast and unicast.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"6d3a6747-8bf5-4b5e-8432-f5c70a687ed4">
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"34707b91-c8f2-4a13-b=
83e-f0956234a591" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"19db6b1345f7"><strong>Update daemon</strong></p></td>
<td data-highlight-colour=3D"#ffffff" data-local-id=3D"7847f001-031d-490d-a=
652-cd0dbc45c7e9" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"41c265fc7d5e">Honors the configured HTTP proxy when download=
ing applications.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"34ad4089fc82">This difference can lead to connectivity issue=
s. For example:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"8deee226-0ff0-48f0-a154-250b5a35f282">
<li local-id=3D"48212015-14c8-4123-9b98-524b1ea627fd">
<p local-id=3D"a5bcf8838911">Discovery identifies a peer that has the requi=
red application.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"543ef84d-08bc-4d99-86cc-f28d91fc4f82">
<p local-id=3D"5235c535d03c">The update daemon attempts to download the app=
lication.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0653549c-7407-4982-89f8-e7958cd2a055">
<p local-id=3D"297a1671a005">The request is routed through the configured p=
roxy.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"82eff957-2ea9-44dc-8094-b59b1b3a80a5">
<p local-id=3D"f0bc9341db68">The proxy cannot route the request back to the=
 local network.</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"4ea724cbbc39">Result: the peer update fails.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"23e94fea06b8" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-Workaround">Workaround</h3>
<p local-id=3D"b2959a189d42">To prevent peer-to-peer traffic from being rou=
ted through the proxy, add the local subnet(s) to the <strong>No Proxy for<=
/strong> configuration:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"b4aa7b2b-a875-41b6-bf95-f0a5bc6978bf">
<li local-id=3D"9a1e677a-81e9-4263-b271-5f12e779ec0d">
<p local-id=3D"768c288a1441">Go to <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https=
://kb.igel.com/en/igel-os-base-system/current/proxy-configuration-in-igel-o=
s-12" rel=3D"nofollow"><strong>Network &gt; Proxy &gt; Manual proxy configu=
ration</strong></a><strong>.</strong></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a816cac5-0406-4e3a-8995-154f887974af">
<p local-id=3D"d1ecb6ba08c7">Find the <strong>No Proxy for </strong>paramet=
er.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"329d4888-fbd7-4f5b-9581-11ff3873a838">
<p local-id=3D"d48d6c4b93aa">Add the CIDR of the subnet, for example:</p></=
li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">192.168=
.1.0/24
10.0.0.0/16</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"cb12cb42d6e4">This ensures that peer-to-peer HTTP traffic is=
 sent directly to local devices.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"3b3cd40fe4a7" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-AlternativeConfigurations">Alternative Configurations</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"686287eae8f0" id=3D"HowtoConfigureDistributedPeerUpdatewith=
IGELOS12Devices-UsingOnlyaSubsetofDevicesasPeerServers">Using Only a Subset=
 of Devices as Peer Servers</h3>
<p local-id=3D"aff3bf8a1904">You can configure a subset of devices as serve=
rs and the rest as clients.</p>
<p local-id=3D"cd7fda61970d">Efficiency drawbacks of this configuration:</p=
>
<ul local-id=3D"59655d64-b44b-45a2-978c-3d82ac4466f6">
<li local-id=3D"b24895f6-5a4d-4c38-998b-c2a85ed0d822">
<p local-id=3D"ec52f39257e0">The UMS assigns applications without consideri=
ng which devices are servers.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fbbb0358-bbf7-4696-aa6e-4a4343b3eba6">
<p local-id=3D"78db87895550">It is more likely that a client=E2=80=91only d=
evice is elected first to use fallback.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"69020be2-227c-418e-bb67-bfe2f2f0ac69">
<p local-id=3D"5f115a451579">Due to the election protocol:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"894d41ce-fc71-4af6-b667-0537c6842801">
<li local-id=3D"c64a5e4b-d739-4ea3-97ba-c5fc29649fc7">
<p local-id=3D"bf0c580f4ae5">only one device at a time downloads from the f=
allback repository</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"28e7b67c-2b40-46a7-9bba-4e54a6be9825">
<p local-id=3D"0bbefa67a1ef">if the elected device is client=E2=80=91only, =
it cannot share the application with others</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"29cf3dab-425d-4439-9b24-8ce3338094af">
<p local-id=3D"baba709bb193">this significantly slows down distribution</p>=
</li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"82962fd8ca8e">To configure this model:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"1ab50fa3-175c-4049-b190-926fc36e9b43">
<li local-id=3D"e9e00f9e-e000-45a2-8b43-573007ae09ba">
<p local-id=3D"e8f0de516a4e">Create a profile for the servers.</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"bb531cfd6997">&nbsp;</p>
<ol start=3D"2" local-id=3D"7f790bb4-8143-467f-acc0-96a2f77c07f5">
<li local-id=3D"bf386b7c-1cdc-4660-966f-5b169957e11d">
<p local-id=3D"17fdcac5021d">Apply the following configurations:</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"831" data-layout=3D"align-start" data-local-id=
